For EDME applicants\nAffiche les pages de m\u00eame niveau\nFor EDME applicants\nFor EDME PhD Students\nEDME People\nEDME Published theses\nEDME Awards\nEDME How to apply?\nAffiche les pages de m\u00eame niveau\nEDME How to apply?\nEDME Alumni testimonials\nEDME Affiliated labs & Research expertise\nEDME Brochure\nAbout\nEducation\nResearch\nInnovation\nSchools\nCampus\nIn the same section\nEDME How to apply?\nEDME Alumni testimonials\nEDME Affiliated labs & Research expertise\nEDME Brochure\nEDME How to apply?\nEDME application deadlines:\n15th April\n15th December\nEPFL is committed to increasing the diversity of the work environment and strongly encourages women and underrepresented minorities to apply.\nEPFL PhD admission criteria & application\nEDME Applications \u2013 FAQ\nAre TOEFL and GRE certificates obligatory?\nThey are not obligatory, but you must be aware that all courses are held in English and that an excellent level of English is required for your thesis work.\nWhen can I expect a decision of the program if I am admitted or not?\nYou will normally get an answer within 3-6 weeks after the application deadline.\nI have received an e-mail saying that I fulfil the requirements of eligibility. What do I have to do now?\nOnce you have received an e-mail saying that you are eligible, you have 12 month to find a thesis director and a research assistantship in a lab. Your admission becomes definitive once you have found the thesis director as well as a research assistantship position.\nHow do I proceed to find a thesis director and a research assistantship position?\nThere are different possibilities. You may contact directly one of the program\u2019s thesis directors (you will find the complete list on our website) to check if he has got any open positions in his lab and if he would be interested in working with you. You may also check the website of the human resources department where you find open PhD positions. It may also be that you will be contacted of one of our thesis directors because he is interested in hiring you after having seen your application dossier.\nFor any further questions: [email protected]\nAbout\nOrganization and identity\nAssociated Campuses\nData\nPresidency\nVice Presidencies\nWorking at EPFL\nRecruiting EPFL Talents\nEquality, Diversity, Inclusion\nRespect\nSustainability\nNews & Media\nPhilanthropy\nEPFL Alumni\nEducation\nAdmission\nAcademic Calendar\nPreparatory Year (CMS)\nBachelor\nMaster\nDoctorate\nSHS Program\nContinuing Education - Extension School\nStudy Management\nInternational\nTeaching\nEducational Initiatives\nEducation & Science Outreach\nInfrastructures Under Development\nEngaging with Society\nResearch\nMission and Policy\nResearch Domains\nEPFL Research Facilities\nFaculty Members\nSolutions 4 Sustainability - S4S\nAwards and Prizes\nFunding Opportunities\nResearch Management Support\nFrom Lab to Market\nResearch Ethics\nResearch with Animals\nOpen Science\nInnovation\nIndustry Collaboration\nInnovation Initiatives\nStartup Launchpad\nCampus\nServices & Resources\nLibrary\nRestaurants, Shops & Hotels\nSecurity, Prevention & Health\nSports\nCommunity & Support\nChaplaincy\nEvents\nArts & Culture\nAssociations\nVisit EPFL\nMobility & Travel\nSchools & Colleges\nSchool of Architecture, Civil & Environmental Engineering ENAC\nSchool of Basic Sciences SB\nSchool of Engineering STI\nSchool of Computer & Communication Sciences IC\nSchool of Life Sciences SV\nCollege of Management of Technology CDM\nPractical\nServices & Resources\nEmergencies: +41 21 693 3000\nContact\nMap\nFollow EPFL on social media\nFollow us on Facebook\nFollow us on Instagram\nFollow us on LinkedIn\nFollow us on Mastodon\nFollow us on X\nFollow us on Youtube\nAccessibility\nDisclaimer\nPrivacy policy\n\u00a9 2025 EPFL, all rights reserved\nBack to top", "links": [["Skip to content", "https://www.epfl.ch/education/phd/edme-mechanics/edme-how-to-apply/#content"], ["", "https://www.epfl.ch/en/"], ["About", "ht